# Observability

## Objective

Operators and developers must answer: **Is it healthy? What failed? How often?**  -  using evidence the system exposes, not guesswork.

## Requirements

- Meaningful logs at decision points and failures (`logging.mdc`).
- Health or readiness signals where the project has a runtime (HTTP health, status UI, heartbeat files, etc.).
> **If this project has no web/deployment surface:** apply the same principles to the nearest release artifact (binary, package, plugin, mobile build) or skip.
- Metrics/tracing when the project already uses them  -  do not invent Prometheus/cloud stacks unless the project has them.
- Correlate errors with enough context to reproduce.
- Throttle noisy diagnostics in hot paths.

